  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\vec{a}, \\vec{b}$ and $\\vec{c}$ be vectors of equal magnitude such that the angle between $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ is $\\alpha, \\vec{b}$ and $\\vec{c}$ is $\\beta$ and $\\vec{c}$ and $\\vec{a}$ is $\\gamma$. Then the minimum value of $\\cos \\alpha+\\cos \\beta+\\cos \\gamma$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "mnjkw",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9ExpR",
      "text": "$-\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7SW9C",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dmXhW",
      "text": "$-\\frac{3}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $|\\mathrm{a}|=|\\overline{\\mathrm{b}}|=|\\overline{\\mathrm{c}}|=\\lambda$\nWe have, $\\overline{\\mathrm{a}} \\cdot \\overline{\\mathrm{b}}=\\lambda^2 \\cos \\alpha, \\quad \\overline{\\mathrm{~b}} \\cdot \\overline{\\mathrm{c}}=\\lambda^2 \\cos \\beta, \\overline{\\mathrm{c}} \\cdot \\overline{\\mathrm{a}}=\\lambda^2 \\cos \\gamma$\nNow, $|\\bar{a}+\\bar{b}+\\bar{c}| \\geq 0$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow 3 \\lambda^2+2 \\lambda^2(\\cos \\alpha+\\cos \\beta+\\cos \\gamma) \\geq 0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\cos \\alpha+\\cos \\beta+\\cos \\gamma \\geq-3 / 2\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
